<h1>sin</h1>
<p>In a right angled triangle sin(val) = Opposite / Hypotenuse where val is one of the three angles.</p>
<p class="note"><b></b><strong>NOTE</strong>: This function takes a value in radians not degrees.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">sin(val);</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th><th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>val</td><td><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></td>
<td>The angle (in radians) to return the sine of.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">val = sin( pi/2 );</p>
<p>This will set val to 1.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
